abel":"Approach 20","number":20,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]}],"assets":[],"contentBlocks":[{"sequence":0,"text":"## Problem Statement\n\nThe INI file format is a de facto standard for configuration files. INI files are simple text files with a basic structure. They are commonly associated with Microsoft Windows, but are also used on other platforms.\n\nEach line in INI-file stands for key-value mapping or defines new section. A key-value line has a format \" key=value \",where key ΓÇö is the name of some property, and value ΓÇö it's value. It is possible that it will be spaces from the both sides of key and/or value , the spaces should be ignored.\n\nA section line has a format \" [section] \". It means that all key-value lines after it define properties of the specified section. Of cause, the following section line changes the current section. A section line may have spaces around any of brackets.\n\nAlso you should ignore comment lines ΓÇö the first non-space character of comment line is \" ; \".\n\nYou task is to write the program which will format given INI-file in a special way: \n\n \n- first, print key-value lines which do not belong to any section; \n- print all the sections in the lexicographical (alphabetical) order of their names; \n- inside each of two previous items, order key-value lines lexicographically by \" key \"; \n- if there are more than one key-value lines with the same key inside a single section (or outside any sections), leave only one line (which appears later in the input data); \n- remove all redundant spaces and lines.\n\n## Input\n\nThe first line contains single integer n ( 1ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë n ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë510 ) ΓÇö the number of lines in given INI-file.\n\nThe rest of the input contains a valid INI-file in n lines. Values of section , key and value contain only Latin letters, digits, \" . \" and/or \" - \".\n\nEach line has length not exceeding 255 characters and not less than 1 character. The total length of all the lines doesΓÇÖt exceed 10000.\n\n## Output\n\nPrint formatted INI-file.\n\n## Examples\n\nExample 1:\n```\n11\na= 1\nb=a\na = 2\n ; comment\n[z]\n1=2\n[y]\n2=3\n[z]\n2=1\n[w]\n```\n```\na=2\nb=a\n[w]\n[y]\n2=3\n[z]\n1=2\n2=1\n```","type":"text"}],"contestId":72,"index":"B","memoryLimit":"256 megabytes","name":"INI-file","problemKey":"72-B","rating":null,"tags":[],"timeLimit":"5 seconds","url":"https://codeforces.com/contest/72/problem/B"},{"approaches":[{"label":"Approach 1","number":1,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 2","number":2,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 3","number":3,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 4","number":4,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 5","number":5,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 6","number":6,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 7","number":7,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 8","number":8,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 9","number":9,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 10","number":10,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 11","number":11,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 12","number":12,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 13","number":13,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 14","number":14,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 15","number":15,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 16","number":16,"